# Day 9/60 — From MVP to Enhanced Product

## Objective

Learn how iterative prompting can improve AI-generated applications.

## Task

Build an MVP version of NutriScope using Claude.

After generating the initial version, use a second enhancement prompt to improve the application and compare the results.

## Process

1. Generate MVP application
2. Save generated HTML
3. Review strengths and weaknesses
4. Apply enhancement prompt
5. Generate improved version
6. Compare both outputs

## What I Learned

### MVP First

The purpose of an MVP is not perfection.

The purpose is validation and functionality.

### Iteration Creates Better Products

The enhanced version benefited from:

* Additional requirements
* Better guidance
* Feedback from the first version

### AI Accelerates Product Evolution

Instead of rebuilding everything manually, Claude was able to improve the existing foundation.

## Comparison

### Version 1 (MVP)

* Core functionality
* Basic UI
* Initial feature set

### Version 2 (Enhanced)

* Improved user experience
* Additional features
* Better structure
* More polished output

## Biggest Insight

The quality of a product often depends on the quality of iteration.

Prompt → Build → Review → Improve

This cycle is more effective than trying to create the perfect solution in a single prompt.

